WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:36.620
<b>The Six Vegapunks</b>

3
00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:41.080
Cause you couldn't
run if you wanted to.

4
00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:52.330
Hakugan, get
to the Polar Tang!

5
00:01:56.510 --> 00:02:03.520
Roger! Shachi, penguin,
into the sea! Leave it to us!

6
00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:12.550
What the hell?

7
00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:16.980
Amputate!

8
00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:31.910
Was that an awakened
technique?

9
00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.690
When did you
learn to do that?

10
00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:36.510
Yes, you did it, Captain.

11
00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:40.200
No, not yet.

12
00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:43.320
Drinking bastard,
you fake your spider!

13
00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:44.630
Ha!

14
00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:46.380
Dribble!

15
00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:48.120
Ha!

16
00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:20.670
He's a monster!

17
00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:35.480
Say it ain't so.

18
00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:38.430
Strong, you were
taken too soon.

19
00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:40.170
How cool!

20
00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:41.980
He's galloping
through heaven now.

21
00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:42.860
Ha ha ha!

22
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.760
Payback time!

23
00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:52.720
Hey, look up!

24
00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.250
There's something falling!

25
00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:56.930
Everybody run!

26
00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:58.940
The apples are bombs!

27
00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:21.480
Nah.

28
00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:25.740
We were born and raised at the coldest
part in the North Blue, you know.

29
00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:28.540
You may be tough, but there's
no way you can beat us at sea!

30
00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:30.290
We're about to sink your ship!

31
00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:35.800
Prepare to attack!

32
00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:37.190
Yeah!

33
00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:56.620
Jean Bart!

34
00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:57.670
Three o'clock!

35
00:04:58.010 --> 00:04:58.840
A sniper!

36
00:04:58.920 --> 00:04:59.720
Hmm.

37
00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:02.300
Get ready to block!

38
00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:03.080
I'm on it!

39
00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.400
Interesting.

40
00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:15.570
His defenses may
prove hard to break.

41
00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:17.940
K.

42
00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:18.870
Room!

43
00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:19.710
K.

44
00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:20.620
Rool, go!

45
00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:26.700
K.

46
00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:27.610
Rool, go!

47
00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.010
Huh?

48
00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:33.720
Was that supposed
to hurt you, idiot?

49
00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.000
Shock feeler.

50
00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:39.550
Huh?

51
00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.170
Stop!

52
00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:46.900
Hmm.

53
00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:48.160
Predictable.

54
00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.670
You can't just charge
in without a strategy.

55
00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:51.700
Now, warp.

56
00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:53.540
Oh.

57
00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:57.060
Commodore, would you
like to return to the ship?

58
00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:57.610
Huh?

59
00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:58.560
You kidding me?

60
00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:00.340
I'm just getting started here!

61
00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:01.880
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!

62
00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:03.480
Very well, then.

63
00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:04.360
Warp!

64
00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:05.620
Pfft!

65
00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:06.490
Ha!

66
00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:15.080
Ha!

67
00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:17.330
It's Blackbeard!

68
00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:20.990
All your top officers
have devil fruit powers.

69
00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:22.310
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!

70
00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:24.990
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!

71
00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:28.090
That means all your best fighters
are weak against the sea!

72
00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:30.010
Ha ha ha ha ha!

73
00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:34.070
After seeing the kind of power we've got,
you don't think that's a fair trade.

74
00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:34.890
Room!

75
00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:35.770
Go!

76
00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:39.650
Takt!

77
00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:48.460
K.

78
00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:49.340
Room!

79
00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:57.150
Enemy attack from below!

80
00:06:57.230 --> 00:06:59.270
Bastards are trying
to sink our ship!

81
00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:02.020
How the hell are they
this strong at sea?

82
00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:15.590
This is wild!

83
00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:17.600
Hmm?

84
00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:18.730
Hmm?

85
00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:19.560
Who's that?

86
00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:22.910
All they're doing is
shaking us around a bit.

87
00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:24.470
It won't last long.

88
00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:27.060
No one in the world can stand
up against our commodore.

89
00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:34.020
If Mama is still alive, you won't
be talking that way much longer.

90
00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:36.980
<b>Charlotte Pudding</b>
<b>Big Mom Pirates</b>

91
00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:38.690
Ha ha ha ha!

92
00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:43.400
If she's alive, we're fighting
the guy who killed her right now!

93
00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:47.900
That old bat and her era are as dead
as your hopes of getting out of here!

94
00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:53.120
A short time ago on Cacao Island,
two intruders suddenly appeared in...

95
00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.570
Chocolat Town, where
Pudding resigned.

96
00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:23.290
The goal of the intruders
was to abduct Pudding.

97
00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:26.900
They were from
the Blackbeard Pirates.

98
00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:30.060
One was the longtime
member of Van Ogre.

99
00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:33.020
The other... was Kuzan.

100
00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:36.900
I know what you're expecting.

101
00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:40.270
But if you think you can force
my hand, you're mistaken.

102
00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:42.930
You'll never get
what you want.

103
00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:55.590
Black Vortex!

104
00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:02.140
Reports say that Blackbeard and Trafalgar
Law are clashing at Winter Island in the...

105
00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:02.770
New World.

106
00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:05.460
That's the problem
with being fleet admiral.

107
00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:09.440
I have to sit here and wait,
instead of wringing their necks.

108
00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:13.700
<b>Future Island, Egghead</b>

109
00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:16.770
Huh.

110
00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:22.630
Okay, that was weird, but I
think we're in the clear now.

111
00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:24.440
Jeez, Bonney.

112
00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:29.470
<b>Luffy, 70 Years Old</b>
<b>(In One Possible Future)</b>

113
00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:29.650
If you made me any older, my bones
would have turned to dust when I fell down.

114
00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:32.880
I get why you're upset.

115
00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:35.530
But pacifistas are dangerous.

116
00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:40.200
And there's lots of them, so you better
get used to watching us beat your dad's ass.

117
00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:41.030
I'm sorry.

118
00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:41.600
Luffy!

119
00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:42.970
That's enough.

120
00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:45.270
I know this is hard, Bonney.

121
00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:46.430
I really do.

122
00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:48.040
But we've dealt
with pacifistas.

123
00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:50.650
Pacifistas in the past,
so just trust us, okay?

124
00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:57.790
Also, if it's not too much trouble,
please turn me back before I die.

125
00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:01.840
I should have thought of this.

126
00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:05.530
Kuma was a normal human before
they started cloning him, after all.

127
00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:07.900
Of course he'd have
a family out there.

128
00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:11.620
Let me get something
straight with you, Bonney.

129
00:10:12.390 --> 00:10:13.800
Please don't be offended.

130
00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:17.080
But I heard that Kuma was the Wicked
King of the Sorbet Kingdom.

131
00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:20.170
Who was expelled by its people
and became a pirate.

132
00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:22.840
Later, he joined up
with the Revolutionary Army.

133
00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:26.510
But was arrested by the Navy
and sentenced to life in prison.

134
00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:30.320
But Doctor Vegapunk
took an interest in him.

135
00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:33.130
He saw potential
in his unique physiology.

136
00:10:33.220 --> 00:10:37.390
And so, Kuma was allowed to return
to the seas as one of the Seven Warlords.

137
00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:41.110
But he had to agree to cloning
and body augmentation, too.

138
00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:43.500
Is that correct?

139
00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:45.320
Yes.

140
00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:48.570
The Warlord part and the cloning
part do make sense to me.

141
00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:50.380
But the cyborg part?

142
00:10:50.470 --> 00:10:52.040
That's like a death sentence.

143
00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:56.080
No one would agree to have
their whole mind taken away like that.

144
00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:57.660
I don't know his crimes.

145
00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:00.510
So I don't know what
kind of deal he agreed to.

146
00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:04.720
But they called him Kuma the Tyrant
and gave him a life sentence.

147
00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:09.530
That's a lie!

148
00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:11.030
My dad wasn't a tyrant!

149
00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:13.370
And I'm positive that he
hated the world government.

150
00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:15.090
He'd never help
them by choice!

151
00:11:15.170 --> 00:11:17.470
They did these things
to him against his will!

152
00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:19.150
Are you trying to kill us?

153
00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:21.420
You know I can't
move fast anymore!

154
00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:23.850
But that weapon was
pretty cool, huh?

155
00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:25.680
Bless my bones!

156
00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:27.330
Was that a beam saber?

157
00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:30.520
There isn't much
that works here.

158
00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:32.840
All these must be
rejected inventions.

159
00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:34.530
But this one's good.

160
00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:37.170
Vegapunk has to pay.

161
00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:39.700
He committed murder
in the name of science!

162
00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:55.460
My father said he came from
a special race of people.

163
00:11:57.060 --> 00:11:57.660
Fine!

164
00:11:57.660 --> 00:11:58.560
So what?

165
00:11:58.640 --> 00:12:01.400
That doesn't give people
the right to experiment on him!

166
00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:04.060
That doesn't give them
the right to erase his mind!

167
00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:04.940
Yeah!

168
00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:05.680
Tell him!

169
00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:06.970
A special race, huh?

170
00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:09.710
Bonney...

171
00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:13.050
You forgot to turn me back.

172
00:12:19.780 --> 00:12:21.080
We can fly!

173
00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:23.930
<b>Team Sunny</b>

174
00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:24.020
But you gotta make us
one of these, Franky!

175
00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:25.140
So cool!

176
00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:30.010
Vegaforce-01 is propelled
by the jets on its back.

177
00:12:30.010 --> 00:12:32.780
But it's kept afloat by
an anti-gravity device.

178
00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:33.890
Oh dang!

179
00:12:33.970 --> 00:12:35.070
That sounds sweet!

180
00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:37.940
It's only possible because
of the air regulation on the island.

181
00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:39.790
But I want to take
it worldwide!

182
00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:42.050
Whoa!

183
00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:42.600
A city!

184
00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:43.770
It's huge!

185
00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:47.430
I've never seen architecture
like that before.

186
00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:49.000
And up we go!

187
00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:56.950
Hey!

188
00:12:57.030 --> 00:12:57.560
Look!

189
00:12:57.560 --> 00:12:59.240
There's a giant
monster down there!

190
00:12:59.240 --> 00:12:59.840
Oh man!

191
00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:01.190
This is amazing!

192
00:13:01.270 --> 00:13:02.740
And another giant robot!

193
00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:03.510
How many of them got it?

194
00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:06.340
Franky, Franky, Franky,
check out the flying fish!

195
00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:08.700
Do they have
anti-gravity devices too?

196
00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:10.580
It's straight out
of a Sci-Fi story!

197
00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:11.460
You bet it is!

198
00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:14.590
We specialize in building
the future here!

199
00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:18.920
This is the future island!

200
00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:19.830
Egghead!

201
00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:25.990
Above the clouds is
the laboratory level, Labophase.

202
00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:28.730
Below is the factory
level, Fabriophase.

203
00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:31.380
That's where all the workers
and researchers live.

204
00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:35.060
Your captain's down there breaking
stuff like a caveman in a cryo center.

205
00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:36.830
I'm glad to know he's all right.

206
00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:45.700
Alright!

207
00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:46.580
We're here!

208
00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:49.680
<b>Labophase
Future Island, Egghead</b>

209
00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:50.060
What kind of cool stuff
are we gonna see next?

210
00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:50.620
Hey!

211
00:13:50.620 --> 00:13:51.350
What gives?

212
00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:52.610
Aren't you guys coming?

213
00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:53.610
We gotta go!

214
00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:55.070
I'm on ship watch.

215
00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:56.050
Me as well.

216
00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:57.260
Can't take risks.

217
00:13:57.340 --> 00:13:58.820
I don't trust that woman.

218
00:13:59.590 --> 00:14:00.310
Course not.

219
00:14:00.390 --> 00:14:01.460
You're an asshole.

220
00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:03.440
Don't listen to him, Lilith!

221
00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:05.130
We all think you're great!

222
00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.010
What is it?

223
00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:10.840
Try it and see.

224
00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:12.390
You mean just step on it?

225
00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:16.870
It's just like Skypiea!

226
00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:17.440
Yep.

227
00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:18.410
Well, I wanna try!

228
00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:19.870
Me too!

229
00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:22.680
This is awesome!

230
00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:25.160
It really takes me back!

231
00:14:25.240 --> 00:14:27.220
This is the first time for me,
but I'm diggin' it!

232
00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:28.980
I wish I could have
been there!

233
00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:31.400
So did Vegapunk make
these clouds, too?

234
00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:32.010
Uh-huh.

235
00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:33.370
Not too shabby, right?

236
00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:37.910
You can probably tell, but by controlling
the island's air systems, I was able

237
00:14:37.990 --> 00:14:41.870
to modify the density of pyrobroin and water
vapor in the condensation nuclei

238
00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:44.800
and recreate the island clouds
and sea clouds of Skypiea!

239
00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:46.860
Those have gotta
be made up words.

240
00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:49.630
And this is
the entrance to the lab!

241
00:14:49.710 --> 00:14:50.540
Awesome!

242
00:14:51.310 --> 00:14:52.840
It's huge!

243
00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:57.400
You'll need to put on research
suits before you go in.

244
00:14:57.400 --> 00:15:00.780
There are changing rooms
through the trancos on the sides.

245
00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:03.670
Welcome.

246
00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:06.260
Please choose
your preferred clothing style.

247
00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:08.740
Okay, but how do I do that?

248
00:15:15.210 --> 00:15:16.370
It's touching me!

249
00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:19.410
Pull the levers on your dom
shoes to adjust the size!

250
00:15:19.490 --> 00:15:21.200
They'll fit any type of foot!

251
00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:22.750
These things, right?

252
00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:25.010
I don't know, they
look pretty bulky.

253
00:15:25.740 --> 00:15:27.120
They're so light!

254
00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:30.390
And adorable!

255
00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:33.850
Wow, that's a killer
look, Robin!

256
00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:34.480
Love it!

257
00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:36.130
So these clothes
can reshape?

258
00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:37.890
I bet they could strangle
us to death.

259
00:15:37.890 --> 00:15:39.620
Why would you
even say that?

260
00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:42.910
Oh yeah!

261
00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:44.530
Future Usopp
coming through!

262
00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:46.000
Vegapunk is the man!

263
00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:48.090
His clothes even fit cyborgs!

264
00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:49.500
Super!

265
00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:52.790
Mine's just a normal
Aloha shirt.

266
00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:56.260
But who cares about me?

267
00:15:56.340 --> 00:15:58.190
You ladies look nice!

268
00:15:58.270 --> 00:15:59.820
It's different, but it's comfy.

269
00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:01.820
You look ready
to kick ass, Robin!

270
00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:02.400
Do I?

271
00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:03.670
How about me?

272
00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:05.690
You look like a perv
in any outfit!

273
00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:07.270
You're making me blush!

274
00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:12.230
Some say that foresight
is a genius's blessing.

275
00:16:12.310 --> 00:16:14.640
Though I'm inclined
to call it a curse.

276
00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:18.150
You know I can't stand it when
you talk in riddles, Vegapunk.

277
00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:19.350
Then I'll be frank.

278
00:16:21.060 --> 00:16:22.670
I'm going to die soon.

279
00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:24.660
What are you talking about?

280
00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:26.590
Is that supposed
to be a joke?

281
00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:29.460
I just wanted you to know
before it happens.

282
00:16:29.850 --> 00:16:30.790
Goodbye, Dragon.

283
00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:35.270
So, why didn't you go
along with the others?

284
00:16:35.350 --> 00:16:37.370
I'm on standby
to go rescue them.

285
00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:38.640
It's a government island.

286
00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:40.660
They're probably
walking into a trap.

287
00:16:41.570 --> 00:16:43.860
You know, I had
the exact same thought.

288
00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:45.710
Now, would you
care for some tea?

289
00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:46.410
Sure.

290
00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:47.420
Thanks, pal.

291
00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:49.400
Excuse me, good sirs!

292
00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:50.800
Why are you still here?

293
00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:51.580
Whoa!

294
00:16:51.590 --> 00:16:52.120
Wait!

295
00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:53.150
Don't be so cruel!

296
00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:56.990
I know the deal was that you'd give
me a ride anywhere outside of Wano,

297
00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:58.600
but I can't get off here!

298
00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:01.460
As you said,
it's a government island!

299
00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:03.210
I'm not exactly welcome!

300
00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:06.130
I appreciate you helping out
our captain, but we're done.

301
00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:07.070
Get lost.

302
00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:10.390
You're gonna pay
for this someday!

303
00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:14.760
<b>At the Lab</b>

304
00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:19.460
The stairs move?

305
00:17:19.840 --> 00:17:20.890
Hell yeah!

306
00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:24.530
So, riding these stairs in style!

307
00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:28.100
Like climbing
a soap yesterday!

308
00:17:28.180 --> 00:17:30.110
The steps are pouring
out from the ground!

309
00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:31.290
This is so crazy!

310
00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:35.370
How does this thing work?

311
00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:36.520
What's it run on?

312
00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:39.360
Everything on the island
is powered by fire.

313
00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:41.990
Flames can be converted
to all forms of energy.

314
00:17:42.070 --> 00:17:44.230
So you need
natural resources?

315
00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:48.370
I've done a lot of research on what
matter is most efficient to burn.

316
00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:53.340
But what I really want is an undying
flame, so I can make a sun!

317
00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:54.710
Make a sun?

318
00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:02.640
You're walking into a wall!

319
00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:05.340
Huh?

320
00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:07.420
Open the wall thingy!

321
00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:09.290
Just walk through it like I did!

322
00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:11.310
Trust your brains,
not your eyes!

323
00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:13.520
Lilith!

324
00:18:14.730 --> 00:18:16.380
Why are you yelling, Edison?

325
00:18:14.790 --> 00:18:15.590
Lilith!

326
00:18:18.220 --> 00:18:21.050
Lilith, my evil queen!

327
00:18:24.980 --> 00:18:25.970
I can't hear anything.

328
00:18:25.970 --> 00:18:26.820
Did she leave us?

329
00:18:28.010 --> 00:18:29.190
That's good, Edison!

330
00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:31.110
I wouldn't worry.

331
00:18:31.190 --> 00:18:34.280
If he had really been decapitated,
there'd be blood everywhere.

332
00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:36.000
Thank you for that
absolutely terrible...

333
00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:37.290
Terrifying analysis!

334
00:18:37.790 --> 00:18:38.690
Sanji!

335
00:18:38.770 --> 00:18:39.740
You still alive?

336
00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:40.990
I'm fine.

337
00:18:41.070 --> 00:18:42.660
You can just walk
right through.

338
00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:44.560
I better not break my nose.

339
00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:45.440
Let me try!

340
00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:47.460
Neat!

341
00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:48.620
Not you too!

342
00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:49.330
Bye, Lisa!

343
00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:52.550
I passed through.

344
00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:53.870
But how?

345
00:18:56.310 --> 00:18:57.140
Fwaaah!

346
00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:03.490
Jeez, why are you
trying to confuse me?

347
00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:04.400
Heh heh!

348
00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:09.070
It's totally solid when
you go through!

349
00:19:09.150 --> 00:19:10.040
Why?

350
00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:11.950
How does this even work?

351
00:19:12.030 --> 00:19:13.880
Wait, where did Lilith go?

352
00:19:14.430 --> 00:19:15.480
Hello?

353
00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:17.490
Walk straight ahead!

354
00:19:17.910 --> 00:19:18.810
Who's there?

355
00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:21.970
Oh, I'm Vegapunk Edison,
at your service!

356
00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:23.290
Welcome to the lab.

357
00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:24.840
I'll guide you from here.

358
00:19:29.220 --> 00:19:30.380
Keep going.

359
00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:33.950
I don't think I'm ever gonna
figure out this weird place.

360
00:19:34.030 --> 00:19:36.000
I'm gonna hunt for some
future treasure.

361
00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:37.290
Now what would that
be exactly?

362
00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:39.090
Like pretty, pretty flowers.

363
00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:40.670
Made of money.

364
00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:43.460
Are you a little Princess
or a greedy old bag?

365
00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:45.150
Future kick!

366
00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:46.970
Future pain!

367
00:20:00.860 --> 00:20:02.130
Someone's in there.

368
00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:04.460
What?

369
00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:05.130
Hold up!

370
00:20:05.130 --> 00:20:05.930
No way!

371
00:20:06.490 --> 00:20:07.300
It's Jinbe!

372
00:20:08.490 --> 00:20:09.240
It can't be.

373
00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:10.100
He's too young.

374
00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:12.930
And he looks
different somehow.

375
00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:19.220
Okay, the first option.

376
00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:20.470
This is Jinbe's child.

377
00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:21.300
Hmm.

378
00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:23.400
Second option.

379
00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:25.440
Jinbe was turned into a child.

380
00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:26.810
I don't think so.

381
00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:28.120
Third option.

382
00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:29.460
He's a lookalike.

383
00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:31.050
With wings.

384
00:20:31.520 --> 00:20:33.230
And a really weird vibe.

385
00:20:33.990 --> 00:20:34.760
Hey!

386
00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:36.060
Who are you?

387
00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:40.340
He's big.

388
00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:43.460
He might look like a kid,
but he's as tall as the real Jinbe.

389
00:20:43.460 --> 00:20:46.020
I got a bad feeling about this.

390
00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:48.380
Option four!

391
00:20:49.050 --> 00:20:50.100
He's a pacifista!

392
00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:51.240
Yeah!

393
00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:53.450
Ah!

394
00:21:13.890 --> 00:21:16.080
We gotta get out of here!

395
00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:17.940
I knew this had to be
a government trap!

396
00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:18.710
I just knew it!

397
00:21:19.520 --> 00:21:19.880
Jinbe!

398
00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:20.580
Stop it!

399
00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:24.730
He doesn't seem
to recall that name.

400
00:21:24.810 --> 00:21:26.090
Or any of us.

401
00:21:26.170 --> 00:21:27.480
Well, it was worth a shot.

402
00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:29.280
But I guess he's
not our friend.

403
00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:35.850
Jinbe aside,
this still feels wrong.

404
00:21:35.930 --> 00:21:38.990
Sure, he's kinda big,
but he looks like a kid to me.

405
00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:43.030
What?

406
00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:48.140
Devil Fruit Power!

407
00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:51.790
What the hell?

408
00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:54.440
I'm ready to go, Nami!

409
00:21:54.520 --> 00:21:55.460
Are we doing this?

410
00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:56.240
Not yet.

411
00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:57.090
Hold on!

412
00:21:59.620 --> 00:22:00.460
Wait!

413
00:22:00.540 --> 00:22:01.670
I know that power!

414
00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:03.420
But how did he get it too?

415
00:22:07.200 --> 00:22:08.030
Jinbe!

416
00:22:11.570 --> 00:22:12.370
Nami!

417
00:22:18.460 --> 00:22:19.580
Stop it!

418
00:22:19.580 --> 00:22:20.760
Let her go!

419
00:22:24.440 --> 00:22:25.420
Jin... Jinbe...

420
00:22:25.500 --> 00:22:27.470
I said let her go, you bastard!

421
00:22:27.810 --> 00:22:29.370
I don't want to throw hands!

422
00:22:29.450 --> 00:22:33.320
But I will mess you up,
even if Vegapunk is my hero!

423
00:22:33.840 --> 00:22:36.010
Death penalty, it is.

424
00:22:36.090 --> 00:22:42.000
Whether you're Jinbe or not,
I'm gonna make you pay!

425
00:22:51.720 --> 00:22:53.440
I'll show you no mercy.

426
00:22:53.520 --> 00:22:55.390
You've made an enemy of us.

427
00:22:55.860 --> 00:22:57.320
Gigante Fleur!

428
00:23:08.050 --> 00:23:10.130
Sea serpent snapdragon!

429
00:23:17.120 --> 00:23:17.920
Spank!

430
00:23:24.240 --> 00:23:25.070
Shit!

431
00:23:26.820 --> 00:23:27.940
Robin, get back!

432
00:23:30.810 --> 00:23:33.490
That's fishman karate!

433
00:23:33.570 --> 00:23:34.600
Special attack!

434
00:23:34.680 --> 00:23:35.840
Green star!

435
00:23:35.920 --> 00:23:37.520
Skull Bombgrass!

436
00:23:43.640 --> 00:23:44.870
Get it together, Usopp!

437
00:23:44.950 --> 00:23:45.790
You can do this!

438
00:23:45.870 --> 00:23:47.260
He's not the real Jinbe!

439
00:23:50.060 --> 00:23:51.000
Did you get him?

440
00:23:51.510 --> 00:23:52.080
Yeah.

441
00:23:52.080 --> 00:23:53.350
I think he's down.

442
00:23:58.390 --> 00:23:59.210
He's gone!

443
00:23:59.290 --> 00:24:00.860
Oh, come on!

444
00:24:01.220 --> 00:24:02.190
I missed?

445
00:24:02.270 --> 00:24:03.120
How could I miss?

446
00:24:03.150 --> 00:24:04.560
He was right there!

447
00:24:11.010 --> 00:24:11.810
No!

448
00:24:13.020 --> 00:24:13.850
Stay away!

449
00:24:14.430 --> 00:24:16.060
Let go of me!

450
00:24:16.720 --> 00:24:17.740
I'm coming!

451
00:24:18.090 --> 00:24:18.930
Stay back!

452
00:24:19.010 --> 00:24:19.810
I got this one!

453
00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:22.000
Usopp!

454
00:24:22.000 --> 00:24:23.480
Stand perfectly still!

455
00:24:27.740 --> 00:24:28.440
Dammit!

456
00:24:28.480 --> 00:24:29.440
Let me die!

457
00:24:29.520 --> 00:24:30.220
No!

458
00:24:30.300 --> 00:24:32.120
You gotta stand still, bro!

459
00:24:32.200 --> 00:24:33.780
I can't take this shot!

460
00:24:33.860 --> 00:24:36.580
What is this energy
he's using?

461
00:24:37.020 --> 00:24:38.240
It can't be!

462
00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:40.830
Radical!

463
00:24:41.260 --> 00:24:42.320
S-shark!

464
00:24:42.400 --> 00:24:43.230
Dodge now!

465
00:24:45.910 --> 00:24:46.710
Beat!

466
00:24:55.040 --> 00:24:57.000
He can shoot lasers?

467
00:24:57.400 --> 00:24:59.360
What kind of pirate
shoots lasers?

468
00:24:59.440 --> 00:25:02.850
If that had hit S-Shark,
it would have been a catastrophe.

469
00:25:02.650 --> 00:25:06.690
<b>Edison</b>

470
00:25:02.770 --> 00:25:06.690
<b>the Visionary</b>

471
00:25:04.260 --> 00:25:06.380
The seraphim
are still children!

472
00:25:06.460 --> 00:25:07.420
They're not ready for this!

473
00:25:07.420 --> 00:25:09.120
I'm not ready
for laser tests yet!

474
00:25:08.700 --> 00:25:09.050
Now!

475
00:25:09.050 --> 00:25:10.160
What the fulcrum!

476
00:25:10.240 --> 00:25:13.400
Who does that idiot think he is,
shooting up our expensive stuff?

477
00:25:13.400 --> 00:25:16.080
I'm gonna rip his head
off and put it in a jar!

478
00:25:16.160 --> 00:25:17.380
Alright, too evil!

479
00:25:17.460 --> 00:25:17.950
What?

480
00:25:17.950 --> 00:25:20.060
You want me to be
nice to the pirates?

481
00:25:21.440 --> 00:25:21.660
Ha!

482
00:25:21.660 --> 00:25:23.650
Those rats are
gonna die in this lab!

483
00:25:23.730 --> 00:25:25.280
Way too evil!

484
00:25:25.360 --> 00:25:26.580
Come on, S-Shark!

485
00:25:26.660 --> 00:25:28.440
Time to beat them
into the ground!

486
00:25:28.520 --> 00:25:29.710
Activate murder mode!

487
00:25:29.790 --> 00:25:31.000
Oh no!

488
00:25:31.080 --> 00:25:32.100
No murder mode!

489
00:25:32.180 --> 00:25:34.650
Trust me, I have more
than enough test data to...

490
00:25:34.730 --> 00:25:35.430
Oh!

491
00:25:35.860 --> 00:25:36.860
Eureka!

492
00:25:36.940 --> 00:25:38.680
I just thought
of a new invention!

493
00:25:38.760 --> 00:25:39.990
Oh, nice work, buddy!

494
00:25:40.070 --> 00:25:42.470
You go do your thing,
I'll hold down the fort for ya.

495
00:25:42.470 --> 00:25:44.010
I'm leaving you in charge.

496
00:25:44.090 --> 00:25:45.480
Pythagoras, say what?!

497
00:25:45.560 --> 00:25:46.940
All over it, pal.

498
00:25:47.020 --> 00:25:50.230
Data like this is
my morning cup of coffee.

