<b>is</b>

546
00:25:53.240 --> 00:25:54.620
<b>eWi</b>

547
00:25:57.270 --> 00:25:58.550
So much work to be done!

548
00:25:58.630 --> 00:26:00.160
Come, my assistant!

549
00:26:07.740 --> 00:26:09.480
Sweet ontogenesis!

550
00:26:11.260 --> 00:26:12.610
Unbelievable!

551
00:26:12.690 --> 00:26:16.970
The seraphim's attack patterns are
continuing to develop as he grows!

552
00:26:17.050 --> 00:26:21.290
As I hypothesized, it seems that experiences
are stored in their bloodline elements!

553
00:26:21.380 --> 00:26:22.080
Go!

554
00:26:22.380 --> 00:26:24.520
Get those pirates' out!

555
00:26:24.600 --> 00:26:26.090
Come on, S-Shark!

556
00:26:27.060 --> 00:26:28.530
Look at him go!

557
00:26:28.610 --> 00:26:31.500
Oh, they evolve into
war machines so fast!

558
00:26:31.580 --> 00:26:37.940
Heart rate of 90, and his green
blood concentration went up!

559
00:26:38.570 --> 00:26:40.820
Show them who's top
of the food chain!

560
00:26:40.900 --> 00:26:42.850
Make chowder out
of those chumps!

561
00:26:56.050 --> 00:26:56.930
<b>York the Greedy</b>

562
00:27:01.200 --> 00:27:02.570
A cursed stomach!

563
00:27:03.010 --> 00:27:04.630
Why must you rumble so?

564
00:27:06.200 --> 00:27:08.090
These revelations
are too important!

565
00:27:08.170 --> 00:27:09.960
I don't have time
to take a lunch break!

566
00:27:09.960 --> 00:27:10.510
Quick!

567
00:27:10.510 --> 00:27:12.140
Eat something for me, York!

568
00:27:15.010 --> 00:27:15.840
Yay...

569
00:27:19.910 --> 00:27:20.690
Yaaah!

570
00:27:20.770 --> 00:27:21.770
Sweet nutrition!

571
00:27:22.390 --> 00:27:24.030
It's sucking into my brain!

572
00:27:24.610 --> 00:27:26.890
The ideas spring forth anew!

573
00:27:30.940 --> 00:27:32.670
We brought everything
we could grab!

574
00:27:32.670 --> 00:27:33.500
Eat up!

575
00:27:37.980 --> 00:27:39.920
Oh, come on, what
am I, dieting?

576
00:27:40.000 --> 00:27:41.880
Bring more,
please and thank you!

577
00:27:41.960 --> 00:27:43.040
Oh, yes, ma'am!

578
00:27:43.120 --> 00:27:44.670
Right away!

579
00:27:52.650 --> 00:27:54.290
This is the life!

580
00:27:54.370 --> 00:27:55.730
BMI is over 600!

581
00:27:56.210 --> 00:27:57.380
I repeat, BMI is over 600!

582
00:27:57.380 --> 00:27:59.840
I was done anyway!

583
00:27:58.310 --> 00:27:59.110
Oh, relax!

584
00:28:00.510 --> 00:28:02.860
Keep it going, S-Shark!

585
00:28:02.940 --> 00:28:06.190
New battle data keeps
pouring in by the second!

586
00:28:08.490 --> 00:28:11.230
No... no, no, no, no, no!

587
00:28:15.990 --> 00:28:18.210
Let's call a temporary truce!

588
00:28:19.370 --> 00:28:22.670
No, this is no time
to drop a deuce!

589
00:28:22.750 --> 00:28:24.770
Come on, fellas!

590
00:28:24.850 --> 00:28:26.730
Can't you see I'm busy?

591
00:28:33.630 --> 00:28:34.770
Much better!

592
00:28:36.390 --> 00:28:38.130
Digestion Punch!

593
00:28:38.670 --> 00:28:40.350
Take that!

594
00:28:42.570 --> 00:28:45.300
Now for the experimental
phase!

595
00:28:45.380 --> 00:28:48.500
Bring me all the data we
have on devil fruit powers!

596
00:28:48.580 --> 00:28:50.890
Bring devil fruit
data to Pythagoras!

597
00:28:50.970 --> 00:28:53.050
Prepare for a animal
experiment!

598
00:28:53.130 --> 00:28:54.880
To the simulation
room immediately!

599
00:28:56.670 --> 00:28:57.470
Sleepy...

600
00:29:00.660 --> 00:29:03.510
The day isn't over and York
is on her fourth eat!

601
00:29:03.590 --> 00:29:04.290
Sleep!

602
00:29:14.010 --> 00:29:15.130
Hold up!

603
00:29:15.210 --> 00:29:16.980
What's going
on with my feet?!

604
00:29:24.270 --> 00:29:26.710
Seraphim, abort all
attack operations.

605
00:29:27.920 --> 00:29:29.860
Edison, Lilith, Pythagoras...

606
00:29:29.940 --> 00:29:31.580
Your experiment is over.

607
00:29:31.660 --> 00:29:33.850
Oh, well there goes my day.

608
00:29:33.930 --> 00:29:39.200
It's more just getting
to the good part!

609
00:29:39.280 --> 00:29:40.710
Stupid Killjoy!

610
00:29:41.290 --> 00:29:42.090
Eureka!

611
00:29:51.660 --> 00:29:54.220
I don't know what happened,
but I think that guy just saved us.

612
00:29:54.220 --> 00:29:56.540
Whoever he is,
I don't trust him one bit.

613
00:29:56.620 --> 00:29:59.210
He must be the guy
Lilith was talking to.

614
00:29:59.290 --> 00:30:00.040
No way!

615
00:30:00.120 --> 00:30:01.280
Could he be?

616
00:30:01.770 --> 00:30:03.390
I am Dr. Vegapunk.

617
00:30:03.470 --> 00:30:04.730
Shaka the Good.

618
00:30:04.950 --> 00:30:08.040
<b>Shaka the Just</b>

619
00:30:08.890 --> 00:30:10.360
Another Vegapunk?

620
00:30:10.440 --> 00:30:12.490
Kinda overdoing it,
don't you think?

621
00:30:12.570 --> 00:30:15.210
So, you are the famous
Straw Hat crew.

622
00:30:15.290 --> 00:30:16.290
Yeah, pleasure.

623
00:30:16.370 --> 00:30:19.230
Now can you tell us why
our shoes are stuck to the floor?

624
00:30:19.310 --> 00:30:21.240
Dom's shoes are magnetized.

625
00:30:21.320 --> 00:30:23.830
We can control them
remotely inside the lab.

626
00:30:23.910 --> 00:30:25.940
Resistance is futile, I take it.

627
00:30:26.830 --> 00:30:28.830
I cannot trust pirates.

628
00:30:28.910 --> 00:30:31.370
Okay, but are you
really Dr. Vegapunk?

629
00:30:31.450 --> 00:30:33.900
Because you're like
the third one we met today!

630
00:30:33.980 --> 00:30:34.910
Indeed.

631
00:30:34.990 --> 00:30:37.030
We are all Vegapunk.

632
00:30:37.110 --> 00:30:38.360
What does that mean?

633
00:30:38.440 --> 00:30:40.310
How many
Vegapunks are there?

634
00:30:41.260 --> 00:30:42.400
Am I Vegapunk?

635
00:30:42.480 --> 00:30:43.180
What?

636
00:30:43.200 --> 00:30:44.070
No, bro.

637
00:30:44.150 --> 00:30:45.770
Will you stop
embarrassing me?

638
00:30:50.580 --> 00:30:51.380
Tell me.

639
00:30:51.760 --> 00:30:54.630
Does this island look
like the future to you?

640
00:30:54.710 --> 00:30:55.520
What?

641
00:30:55.600 --> 00:30:56.720
Are you kidding me?

642
00:30:57.060 --> 00:30:58.530
Of course it does!

643
00:30:58.610 --> 00:31:00.900
You got mechanical
monsters out in the sea.

644
00:31:00.980 --> 00:31:02.800
Vegaforce-01 flying around.

645
00:31:02.880 --> 00:31:05.030
Air and temperature
regulations everywhere.

646
00:31:05.050 --> 00:31:07.050
This place looks like
the super future.

647
00:31:07.130 --> 00:31:10.210
The city here is like nothing
I've ever seen before.

648
00:31:10.290 --> 00:31:12.780
I want to check out that
tech from top to bottom.

649
00:31:12.860 --> 00:31:14.860
This island's
the freaking bomb!

650
00:31:14.940 --> 00:31:16.950
So don't be a hater, Vega bro.

651
00:31:17.030 --> 00:31:18.270
Let us go explore it.

652
00:31:18.350 --> 00:31:19.960
Pretty please?

653
00:31:20.640 --> 00:31:23.010
It will never surpass
its predecessor.

654
00:31:23.090 --> 00:31:23.920
Huh?

655
00:31:25.500 --> 00:31:27.500
This island is the past.

656
00:31:30.490 --> 00:31:32.310
How could you
call it the past?

657
00:31:33.320 --> 00:31:38.280
Hypothetically speaking, if I told you
there was an advanced kingdom,

658
00:31:38.360 --> 00:31:44.050
much like this island, that existed 900
years ago, would you believe me?

659
00:31:45.050 --> 00:31:46.050
Wait, like 9-0-0?

660
00:31:47.080 --> 00:31:48.680
That's crazy talk, bro!

661
00:31:54.300 --> 00:31:55.170
Chopper, look!

662
00:31:56.000 --> 00:31:57.140
It's really real!

663
00:31:57.220 --> 00:31:58.320
It's not a half of it!

664
00:31:58.710 --> 00:32:00.020
Gotta come check this out!

665
00:32:00.100 --> 00:32:00.870
See that?

666
00:32:00.950 --> 00:32:01.870
It's metal!

667
00:32:05.800 --> 00:32:08.310
Looks impressive,
but it's pretty beat up.

668
00:32:09.460 --> 00:32:11.870
Do you think this thing
used to move around?

669
00:32:11.950 --> 00:32:13.450
Well, that would be a stretch.

670
00:32:13.510 --> 00:32:16.890
Even with this island's tech,
it looks like it's quite old.

671
00:32:16.970 --> 00:32:18.010
Can we ride it?

672
00:32:18.510 --> 00:32:19.210
Yeah!

673
00:32:19.290 --> 00:32:20.120
Great idea!

674
00:32:20.650 --> 00:32:22.120
I'll race you to the top!
